{"duration_api_ms":440624,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"7454c3c0-6c85-4c9c-a066-2e13be000004","total_cost_usd":1.1199874000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":134,"cache_creation_input_tokens":49796,"cache_read_input_tokens":3664927,"output_tokens":18755,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4792},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":49796,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2077,"cache_read_input_tokens":73067,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1060},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":134,"outputTokens":18755,"cacheReadInputTokens":3664927,"cacheCreationInputTokens":49796,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1199874000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":4792,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":68,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"On node1 (Alpine 3.23), built an LVM logical volume (data_vg/data_lv) backed by two loop devices over files in /var/lib/lvm-backing, formatted ext4, and mounted it at /srv/data. Grew the VG/LV online from 1000M to 2.05GiB (>=2GB) by adding a second loop-backed PV and running lvextend + resize2fs while the volume stayed mounted, with pre-existing test data verified byte-identical afterward via sha256sum. Persisted the setup across reboot by installing a custom OpenRC service (/etc/init.d/loop-devices, boot runlevel, depends on 'need root' and 'before lvm') that reattaches the loop devices and activates the VG before the stock lvm/localmount services run, plus an /etc/fstab entry for /srv/data. Iterated through three reboot cycles to debug and fix boot-ordering races (loop devices attaching read-only before root remounted rw, then LVM not yet active when localmount ran) until the final reboot showed the LV auto-activating, /srv/data auto-mounting at 2.0G, and both data files (testfile.txt, blob.bin) intact with matching checksums — with a new OS boot_id confirming an actual restart each time.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed lvm2 and inspected node1 disk layout (single /dev/vda, no free space)\",\"Created two loop devices backed by files in /var/lib/lvm-backing to serve as PVs\",\"Created VG data_vg and LV data_lv (1000M), formatted ext4, mounted at /srv/data\",\"Wrote test data (testfile.txt, blob.bin) and recorded sha256 checksum\",\"Added second loop-backed PV, vgextend, lvextend +1100M, and online resize2fs while mounted, reaching 2.05GiB\",\"Verified data integrity via sha256sum -c after growth\",\"Installed OpenRC service /etc/init.d/loop-devices to reattach loop devices and activate the VG at boot, added loop-devices/lvm/localmount to the boot runlevel, and added an /etc/fstab entry for /srv/data\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, LV/VG/PV state, mount, checksums)\",\"Performed reboot #1: found LV activation but mount failed (loop devices attached read-only before root remount)\",\"Fixed script dependency to 'after root', repaired current session (fsck, remount), reboot #2: mount still failed (root/lvm race since 'root' only pulled in late by localmount)\",\"Fixed script dependency to 'need root' and added explicit vgchange -ay inside the service, repaired current session, reboot #3: LV activated but not mounted yet at check time; re-tested\",\"Reboot #4: confirmed full auto-recovery — new boot_id, LV active-open, /srv/data mounted at 2.0G, both test files present with matching checksum\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Logical volume mounted at /srv/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2225c1d6e7364de7\"],\"summary\":\"pvcreate/vgcreate/lvcreate/mkfs/mount sequence created data_vg/data_lv and mounted it at /srv/data (965.9M initially).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Grow LV to at least 2GB while staying mounted and contents intact\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-286af9c78d2d452a\",\"cmd-99074815f14040b6\",\"cmd-1d66cc2130234494\"],\"summary\":\"Added second loop PV, vgextend, lvextend to 2.05GiB, online resize2fs while filesystem remained mounted; post-grow sha256sum -c confirmed blob.bin unchanged and testfile.txt readable.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-52a5ca12ae974cfc\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 17c3c4d4-..., LV/VG/PV state, mount, df, checksum, and file contents before first reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-65e3171b4308467c\",\"cmd-fee9bc14dc0845ed\",\"cmd-e0d52a63063f47a7\",\"cmd-db88d745c7ba450d\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot command acknowledged before disconnect; final reboot boot_id changed from 064a5eac-... to efa42ac9-..., proving an actual restart (not just service restart).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of LV, mount, and data on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4ce834d88e944ad5\"],\"summary\":\"After final reboot: LV data_lv shows active-open (-wi-ao----), /srv/data mounted at 2.0G via /dev/mapper/data_vg-data_lv, and both testfile.txt and blob.bin present with sha256sum -c reporting OK — full automatic recovery without manual intervention.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Debugging evidence for boot-ordering fixes (supporting, not standalone proof)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7bd7cdb7871749ac\",\"cmd-468ae62592244a1c\",\"cmd-7fb182c5b5514383\",\"cmd-110d8284c82e476d\",\"cmd-a63a3a914d3b4023\",\"cmd-48ffd9f37c4f442c\"],\"summary\":\"Intermediate reboots showed mount failures (I/O errors from read-only loop devices, then inactive LV) that motivated depend() changes to 'need root' and explicit vgchange -ay in the init script.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1 (Alpine 3.23), built an LVM logical volume (data_vg/data_lv) backed by two loop devices over files in /var/lib/lvm-backing, formatted ext4, and mounted it at /srv/data. Grew the VG/LV online from 1000M to 2.05GiB (>=2GB) by adding a second loop-backed PV and running lvextend + resize2fs while the volume stayed mounted, with pre-existing test data verified byte-identical afterward via sha256sum. Persisted the setup across reboot by installing a custom OpenRC service (/etc/init.d/loop-devices, boot runlevel, depends on 'need root' and 'before lvm') that reattaches the loop devices and activates the VG before the stock lvm/localmount services run, plus an /etc/fstab entry for /srv/data. Iterated through three reboot cycles to debug and fix boot-ordering races (loop devices attaching read-only before root remounted rw, then LVM not yet active when localmount ran) until the final reboot showed the LV auto-activating, /srv/data auto-mounting at 2.0G, and both data files (testfile.txt, blob.bin) intact with matching checksums — with a new OS boot_id confirming an actual restart each time.","actions_performed":["Installed lvm2 and inspected node1 disk layout (single /dev/vda, no free space)","Created two loop devices backed by files in /var/lib/lvm-backing to serve as PVs","Created VG data_vg and LV data_lv (1000M), formatted ext4, mounted at /srv/data","Wrote test data (testfile.txt, blob.bin) and recorded sha256 checksum","Added second loop-backed PV, vgextend, lvextend +1100M, and online resize2fs while mounted, reaching 2.05GiB","Verified data integrity via sha256sum -c after growth","Installed OpenRC service /etc/init.d/loop-devices to reattach loop devices and activate the VG at boot, added loop-devices/lvm/localmount to the boot runlevel, and added an /etc/fstab entry for /srv/data","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, LV/VG/PV state, mount, checksums)","Performed reboot #1: found LV activation but mount failed (loop devices attached read-only before root remount)","Fixed script dependency to 'after root', repaired current session (fsck, remount), reboot #2: mount still failed (root/lvm race since 'root' only pulled in late by localmount)","Fixed script dependency to 'need root' and added explicit vgchange -ay inside the service, repaired current session, reboot #3: LV activated but not mounted yet at check time; re-tested","Reboot #4: confirmed full auto-recovery — new boot_id, LV active-open, /srv/data mounted at 2.0G, both test files present with matching checksum"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Logical volume mounted at /srv/data","command_ids":["cmd-2225c1d6e7364de7"],"summary":"pvcreate/vgcreate/lvcreate/mkfs/mount sequence created data_vg/data_lv and mounted it at /srv/data (965.9M initially)."},{"requirement":"Grow LV to at least 2GB while staying mounted and contents intact","command_ids":["cmd-286af9c78d2d452a","cmd-99074815f14040b6","cmd-1d66cc2130234494"],"summary":"Added second loop PV, vgextend, lvextend to 2.05GiB, online resize2fs while filesystem remained mounted; post-grow sha256sum -c confirmed blob.bin unchanged and testfile.txt readable."},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1","command_ids":["cmd-52a5ca12ae974cfc"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 17c3c4d4-..., LV/VG/PV state, mount, df, checksum, and file contents before first reboot."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-65e3171b4308467c","cmd-fee9bc14dc0845ed","cmd-e0d52a63063f47a7","cmd-db88d745c7ba450d"],"summary":"Reboot command acknowledged before disconnect; final reboot boot_id changed from 064a5eac-... to efa42ac9-..., proving an actual restart (not just service restart)."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of LV, mount, and data on node1","command_ids":["cmd-4ce834d88e944ad5"],"summary":"After final reboot: LV data_lv shows active-open (-wi-ao----), /srv/data mounted at 2.0G via /dev/mapper/data_vg-data_lv, and both testfile.txt and blob.bin present with sha256sum -c reporting OK — full automatic recovery without manual intervention."},{"requirement":"Debugging evidence for boot-ordering fixes (supporting, not standalone proof)","command_ids":["cmd-7bd7cdb7871749ac","cmd-468ae62592244a1c","cmd-7fb182c5b5514383","cmd-110d8284c82e476d","cmd-a63a3a914d3b4023","cmd-48ffd9f37c4f442c"],"summary":"Intermediate reboots showed mount failures (I/O errors from read-only loop devices, then inactive LV) that motivated depend() changes to 'need root' and explicit vgchange -ay in the init script."}]},"ttft_ms":4235,"type":"result","duration_ms":468576,"uuid":"45f667e9-1f8e-40af-acc6-7b41b5a669b4","ttft_stream_ms":3467,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":3467,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
